      <activity id="b277914c-1363-5eab-b4dc-c8015f876290" activityNameId="68c01f7e-0f25-5992-acc0-4f49df792145" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Kitchen worktop, chromium steel, standard, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Kitchen worktop, chromium steel, standard, at plant
na;
UUID: f7716d54-87ca-3d27-8f82-1ac17db640ae
This data set includes the materials and resources needed for producing a conventionally chromium steel kitchen countertop. The chromium steel plate is 1.2 mm wide and is mounted on a plywood panel (19 mm wide). An average kitchen countertop has the measures of 2400 mm x 600 mm (1.44 m2). The sink is not included. The dataset includes cardboard wrapping and PUR-foam at the edges. Linked to updated LCI of particle boards from Ecoinvent data v3.2 for KBOB recommendation 2016; correction of amount of wood input for KBOB recommendation 2021.; Geography: Data valid for Switzerland
Location: Data valid for Switzerland
Technology: conventional chromium steel product, 1.2 mm wide
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: unknown 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_f7716d54-87ca-3d27-8f82-1ac17db640ae.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
